This repository is a personal developer profile and contains two
different kinds of material, licensed differently. This split is
deliberate: the generation tooling is generic and useful to anyone,
while the profile's content is personal and commercial branding that
should not be reused as-is.

1. Code (the "tooling")
   Everything under tools/, templates/, and the JSON schema shape used
   by config/ and data/ (i.e., the file structure and field names, not
   the values in them) is licensed under the MIT License below. Copy
   it, adapt it, and use it to build your own generated profile.

2. Content (the "profile")
   Everything else, including but not limited to:
     - the name Anthony Karanja and the ALPHACODE SOLUTIONS brand name
     - the values inside config/profile.json and config/theme.json
     - the project names, descriptions, problem/solution text and
       feature lists inside data/projects.json
     - every generated SVG under assets/ (icons, diagrams, banners,
       stats cards) and README.md itself, since both are derived from
       the content above
   is not licensed for reuse. All rights to this material are reserved
   by Anthony Karanja. If you use this repository as a template for
   your own profile (which the MIT-licensed tooling is meant to
   support), replace all of the content above with your own before
   publishing.

